esry alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What’s it made from?</p></span></div><div data-rid="97d55b97-71c0-4173-bf5e-c4ba33916d75" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-l0up3g"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-bixo17" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden=""><div data-rid="778f2298-17a2-4dc3-a079-5b6b2bf06b43" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-11ne48b"><div data-rid="cd9d6937-8e26-4b3a-abc7-7022292541c6" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-q48nj1 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The Multimat is made from high density polypropylene, knitted mono/mono and fully bound all the way around the mat and peg pointed approximately every half metre.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="2a02a58b-94e9-46f0-aa68-e690a5b2cfe9" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1nt654s" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="0ea3dc86-3866-4a1c-8863-747372c3582f" aria-expanded="false" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1alxizs"><div data-rid="07d99dc1-328e-4690-b808-f71dab6e6320" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-cac8mi alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How does sand not rise to the top of the multimat?</p></span></div><div data-rid="d5591d91-495a-4c7b-88db-72b405944083" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-scaq7"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-138qbzm" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden=""><div data-rid="290f1ff6-64de-447b-b59d-86815835798e" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-18k73jt"><div data-rid="176cc5b6-c34e-4ca1-bee9-6bd5eaaa43a6" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1qnpt29 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>This is due to the dual layers and the law of gravity. The sand and dirt won’t rise to the top of the multimat because the multiple layers create maximum resistance. This stops sand and dirt transferring into the tent, caravan or camper trailer unlike a single layer mat which has no resistance.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="75613be6-c269-4693-bb26-7dc315fa5417" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-8vk20f" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="90869911-51c2-4d00-a84a-7fa9bf04dde0" aria-expanded="false" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-567nav"><div data-rid="8eca98c7-1d6b-4f1c-9832-9b6e5a5fb4a1" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-24ccan alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>CAN I put pegs through the multimat?</p></span></div><div data-rid="72d29aa5-1068-4889-a44d-fe099752507d" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1esiluz"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-1ddvics" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden=""><div data-rid="a35e8d74-3a01-484c-8432-adc9beaf1baa" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1d5jz2v"><div data-rid="c1b30421-f61c-4897-afe3-a2b2c4792699" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1xezgau alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Tent pegs can be pegged into multimat, but not designed to be pegged. The mat material has rip stop technology so it won’t tear or fray if you put a hole in it.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="2035df51-0868-4060-a15a-53dd39a27513" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-c22t0p" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="258d2ca4-85d7-4c47-b720-1944fa8d74ac" aria-expanded="false" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-e36or5"><div data-rid="f05a196c-6a7e-43fd-83c9-5c5fc13a7169" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-98uw7u alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Do I have to peg the multimat into the ground?</p></span></div><picture data-rid="3a0edfd6-e3f0-4e3b-8ba6-1af7b2dd1c54" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-16et26f"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0108/4293/1258/files/Path_Stroke.svg?v=1720522141" class="r-7vkbj6" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="2d9b1bf6-153b-4f56-846b-43b49555f8b4" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-qhwntu"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-1qi1p95" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden=""><div data-rid="02369d89-1ccb-4d1c-a661-b18b2e439479" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1gfkbq7"><div data-rid="b798dbab-37f7-4e08-b8aa-181a2498138a" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1i871ev alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Multimat is designed to be pegged at all D-Ring points for maximum efficiency.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="d0f77b4b-e52a-4ca3-bc50-1811d3c71deb" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1wcd229" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="bd0b3fc6-f932-46aa-a8ee-baac0b5fd340" aria-expanded="false" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-yt18ry"><div data-rid="43843bd0-a1fa-47a2-acaf-d0b9b0e7fffd" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1goi6ln alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Do you include a warranty?</p></span></div><div data-rid="6e0653ac-5d7d-4638-b86a-4470b602a0cd" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1g1c71j"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-1dweulj" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden=""><div data-rid="5805e2e1-c779-437c-88a5-6bef1333ee52" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-y52hfd"><div data-rid="ccbce5e6-84d6-4548-8c24-a1ef04e0c4c2" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-9atc7d alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Multimat has a 12 month warranty from the date of purchase. This is a manufacturer’s warranty eg faulty sewing or material. Faulty products should be returned to the place of purchase together with a copy of the original receipt.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="a6e484b9-f58c-4a13-91e7-dbe7d655dfa1" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1nth1xk" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="74df9771-de29-4d83-8d7e-01db96561e10" aria-expanded="false" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1ti5ok2"><div data-rid="5e079295-957d-4291-b3b8-3136946b59bb" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-yl9uvh alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Will Camp furniture damage the mat?</p></span></div><div data-rid="ea269b67-025a-48c9-aa17-97448a2acaee" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1rktsff"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:100%" class="r-8sodoo" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M1.646 4.646a.5.5 0 0 1 .708 0L8 10.293l5.646-5.647a.5.5 0 0 1 .708.708l-6 6a.5.5 0 0 1-.708 0l-6-6a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.708"></path></svg></div></div><div hidden=""><div data-rid="5392d991-7668-4671-a645-d4ca7669501e" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-10hbuis"><div data-rid="e12dd36e-9f07-468e-a661-fef59e86abb0" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-1acvn3i alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>All good camp furniture have leg protectors or loop legs to protect mat from damage. If legs have plastic protectors, these need to be replaced with rubber protectors to stop sliding.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="304b02d9-4138-43db-805a-19ddccf18389" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0" class="r-dw6l59" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="d08d0139-6857-4edb-99fa-ac7a70ccf0d0" aria-expanded="false" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1uwp9oa"><div data-rid="3dca2ac7-1a8f-4004-a6cb-a9e78aff62ba" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-170n78h alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Will mud ruin the mat?</p></span></div><div data-rid="787349f2-ec3c-4cc8-a896-0f5b18f6d96b" data-replo-repeated-index=".0.0.0.0.0.0.0" class="r-yykfrf"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="curr